      "side": 1,
      "message": "No this test case doesn\u0027t pass with old code. With delay timer set on a network and unregisterAfterReplacement is triggered, we still go ahead and set the permission on the network which is destroyed at netd.\n\nWith this fix, we check if the network is alive now and then set the permission.\n\nThe test case does the same.\n\n1) Create a NA and set delay timer\n2 ) Trigger unregisterAfterReplacement which destroys network with netd first and then disconnects.\n3) Since the network is not alive at netd, permission won\u0027t be set and disconnect will happen without a crash.\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java;l\u003d4710?q\u003dConnectivityService\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject",
